===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*mey- (change)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|comun}}, from {{der|en|xno|comun}}, from {{der|en|fro|comun}} (rare in the {{w|Gallo-Romance languages}}, but reinforced as a [[w:Carolingian|Carolingian]] calque of {{cog|gmw-pro|*gamainī||common}} in {{der|en|fro|-}}), from {{der|en|la|commūnis||common, public, general}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro||*ḱom-moy-ni-s|t=held in common}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*mey-||to exchange, change}}. Displaced native {{cog|enm|imene}}, {{m|enm|ȝemǣne||common, general, universal}} (from {{cog|ang|ġemǣne||common, universal}}), {{cog|enm|mene}}, {{m|enm|mǣne||mean, common}} (also from {{cog|ang|ġemǣne||common, universal}}), {{noncog|enm|samen}}, {{m|enm|somen||in common, together}} (from {{noncog|ang|samen||together}}). {{doublet|en|gmina|mean}}.

