#* {{quote-text|en|year=1768|author={{w|Arthur Murphy (writer)|Arthur Murphy}}|title=Zenobia
|passage=above the vulgar flight of '''common''' souls}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Oliver Twist|volume=II|chapter=XXII|page=35|passage=Mr. Crackit (for he it was) had no very great quantity of hair, either upon his head or face, but what he had was of a reddish dye, and tortured into long corkscrew curls, through which he occasionally thrust some very dirty fingers ornamented with large '''common''' rings.}}
#* {{RQ:Verne Twenty Thousand Leagues|chapter=I|page=3|passage=Merchants, '''common''' sailors, captains of vessels, skippers, […] naval officers of all countries, and the Governments of several states on the two continents, were deeply interested in the matter.}}
